# Post-Update Workflow

Whenever code is modified in this project, follow this sequence:

## 1. Push Updates to Git

After making edits, run:
```bash
git add -A && git status
```
Review changes, then:
```bash
git commit -m "Descriptive message of changes" && git push
```
Use `git_write` permission when pushing.

## 2. Restart the Django Server

- Check if a server is already running (terminals folder or `lsof -i :8000`)
- If running: stop it (Ctrl+C or kill the process), then start fresh
- Start: `python manage.py runserver` (from project root with venv activated)
- Run in background so the user can continue

## 3. Provide Dashboard Links

Always include these links in your response after updates:

| Page | URL |
|------|-----|
| **Owner Dashboard** (homepage) | http://127.0.0.1:8000/ |
| **Dashboard** (alternate) | http://127.0.0.1:8000/dashboard |
| **Admin** | http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/ |
| **Billing** | http://127.0.0.1:8000/billing/ |
| **Jobs** | http://127.0.0.1:8000/jobs/ |

---

**Note:** If the user only asked a question or requested no edits, skip this workflow.
